Step 1: Verify the MariaDB Dump Path

Backups need mariadb-dump.exe. We set this in Phase 1c but let's confirm it's still in place.
powershell

Select-String -Path config\database.php -Pattern "dump_binary_path"

If it prints a path — good, skip to Step 2.

If it prints nothing, open the config and add the dump block:
powershell

notepad++ config\database.php

Find the 'mariadb' => [ connection and add inside it (before the closing ],):
php

        'dump' => [
            'dump_binary_path' => 'C:/Program Files/MariaDB 12.3/bin',
            'use_single_transaction' => true,
            'timeout' => 60 * 5,
        ],

Verify the path is correct:
powershell

dir "C:\Program Files\MariaDB 12.3\bin\mariadb-dump.exe"

If it 404s, find the actual path:
powershell

Get-ChildItem "C:\Program Files\MariaDB*" -Recurse -Filter "mariadb-dump.exe" | Select-Object -First 1 -ExpandProperty FullName

Use the folder portion of the result in the config. Forward slashes, not backslashes.
