Step 3: Create the Backup Batch File

A .bat file is what Windows Task Scheduler will execute. It handles logging and cleanup in one shot.
powershell

notepad++ backup.bat

Create in the project root, paste:
batch

@echo off
REM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
REM  Chula Tiffins — Nightly Backup
REM  Runs from Windows Task Scheduler at 2:00 AM
REM  Writes output to storage\logs\backup.log
REM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

cd /d "C:\Users\RAIPC\tiffin-app"

set PHP="C:\Program Files\php\php.exe"
set LOG="C:\Users\RAIPC\tiffin-app\storage\logs\backup.log"

echo. >> %LOG%
echo ============================================ >> %LOG%
echo Backup started at %date% %time% >> %LOG%
echo ============================================ >> %LOG%

REM Create the backup
%PHP% artisan backup:run --only-db >> %LOG% 2>&1
if %ERRORLEVEL% NEQ 0 (
    echo BACKUP FAILED with error code %ERRORLEVEL% >> %LOG%
)

REM Include uploaded files (images, QR codes, receipts) on Sundays only
for /f "tokens=1" %%a in ('powershell -Command "(Get-Date).DayOfWeek.value__"') do set DOW=%%a
if "%DOW%"=="0" (
    echo Sunday — including files backup >> %LOG%
    %PHP% artisan backup:run --only-files >> %LOG% 2>&1
)

REM Clean old backups
%PHP% artisan backup:clean >> %LOG% 2>&1

echo Backup finished at %date% %time% >> %LOG%

Save and close.

What this does:

    Runs the DB backup every night — small and fast

    Runs the files backup only on Sundays — much heavier, keeps the LAN light on weekdays

    Cleans up old backups per the retention policy

    Logs everything to storage\logs\backup.log

Adjust the paths if your PHP or project location is different. Verify:
powershell

Test-Path "C:\Program Files\php\php.exe"
Test-Path "C:\Users\RAIPC\tiffin-app\artisan"

Both should return True.
Step 4: Test the Batch File Manually

Before scheduling it, run it once by hand:
powershell

.\backup.bat

Wait for it to finish (30 seconds to a few minutes, depending on DB size).

Then check the log:
powershell

Get-Content storage\logs\backup.log -Tail 30

Expected:
text

Backup started at 09/22/2026 14:23:41
Backup completed successfully.
...
Cleanup completed successfully.
Backup finished at 09/22/2026 14:24:02

Verify a backup was created:
powershell

php artisan backup:list

You should see a table showing the backup filename, disk, size, and date.

If the batch file fails, open storage\logs\backup.log and paste the error here. Common causes:

    Wrong mariadb-dump.exe path → check Step 1

    PHP not on the path in the .bat → verify the set PHP= line

    Permissions on storage\app → run once as Admin to seed

Step 5: Create the Windows Task Scheduler Job

Easiest method — one command in an Admin PowerShell:

Right-click PowerShell → Run as Administrator, then paste this single command (replace nothing — paths are exact):
powershell

schtasks /Create /TN "Chula Tiffins Backup" /TR "C:\Users\RAIPC\tiffin-app\backup.bat" /SC DAILY /ST 02:00 /RU SYSTEM /RL HIGHEST /F

What each part does:
Flag	Meaning
/TN "Chula Tiffins Backup"	Task name shown in Task Scheduler
/TR "...backup.bat"	The command to run
/SC DAILY	Schedule: every day
/ST 02:00	Start time: 2:00 AM
/RU SYSTEM	Run as SYSTEM account (no login needed)
/RL HIGHEST	Highest privileges (for file access)
/F	Force overwrite if the task exists

Expected output: SUCCESS: The scheduled task "Chula Tiffins Backup" was successfully created.

Verify it exists:
powershell

schtasks /Query /TN "Chula Tiffins Backup" /V /FO LIST

Should show Status: Ready, Next Run Time: <tomorrow at 2:00 AM>, Run As User: SYSTEM.

Test it immediately (without waiting until 2 AM):
powershell

schtasks /Run /TN "Chula Tiffins Backup"

Then check storage\logs\backup.log for a new entry — it should appear within a minute.
