Step 7: Manual Off-Site Routine (Monthly)

Automated backups protect you from software failures (bugs, bad migrations). They do not protect against hardware failures (disk death, theft, fire).

Once a month, do this:

    Plug in an external USB drive

    Copy the newest backup zip from storage\app\private\<your-app-name>\ to the external drive

    Store the drive somewhere separate from the server

The backup:list command shows you where the files are:
powershell

php artisan backup:list

Consider adding a recurring calendar reminder for the 1st of each month. This single habit will save your business if the production box ever fails.
Step 8: Test a Restore

A backup you've never tested is a backup you don't have. Let's prove it works once.
powershell

php artisan backup:list

Note the most recent filename — something like 2026-09-22-14-23-41.zip. The path shown will tell you where it lives.

Now verify the archive opens:
powershell

Get-ChildItem storage\app\private -Recurse -Filter "*.zip" | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 FullName, Length

If the file is under 1 KB, the backup is empty — something failed. Check storage\logs\backup.log.

If it's several hundred KB or more, do a test restore on a scratch database:

    Create a throwaway DB:

powershell

mysql -u root -p -e "CREATE DATABASE tiffin_restore_test;"

    Extract the zip to a temp folder, then import the SQL inside it:

powershell

Expand-Archive -Path "storage\app\private\Chula Tiffins\*.zip" -DestinationPath "$env:TEMP\tiffin-restore" -Force
dir "$env:TEMP\tiffin-restore"

    Find the .sql file inside and import it:

powershell

mysql -u root -p tiffin_restore_test < "$env:TEMP\tiffin-restore\db-dumps\mariadb-tiffin.sql"

    Confirm tables exist:

powershell

mysql -u root -p tiffin_restore_test -e "SHOW TABLES;"

Should list all 26 tables.

    Clean up:

powershell

mysql -u root -p -e "DROP DATABASE tiffin_restore_test;"
Remove-Item "$env:TEMP\tiffin-restore" -Recurse -Force

If the restore works, your backup pipeline is proven.
